{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "quote", "parent_tag": "04V9", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X} \\rightarrow X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mu_n$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0005": "$S$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4e2d9c78594f07e4b238eb7093291b59d146b9b9373fdb3da1183f844049fb17", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f309884b4c478fa34592f3a1b5327511ab25ea451673a0397de24c806697b523", "source_text": "This paper contains a summary of gerbes and twisted sheaves. If <MATH_0001> is a <MATH_0002>-gerbe with <MATH_0003> a projective relative surface with smooth connected geometric fibers, it is shown that the stack of semistable <MATH_0004>-twisted sheaves is an Artin stack locally of finite presentation over <MATH_0005>. This paper also develops the theory of associated points and purity of sheaves on Artin stacks.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fa8953010f8a54187bcaa81c5f6e1ed38aa2b91e8f55f4ecb1363e964c9fc685", "unit_id": "tag:04V9:item001-quote"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "list_item", "parent_tag": "04V9", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\item Lieblich, Osserman:\n\\emph{", "suffix": "}\n\\cite{lieblich-osserman}\n\\begin{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c49d277e497c6792ce21e8bff33de2033c946c069e454a7d2ddafeed483e4d19", "source_text": "Functorial reconstruction theorem for stacks", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0da077cef486356bb3d55644f62c528cda07feff348ad4e133c5b204536185c5", "unit_id": "tag:04V9:item002"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "quote", "parent_tag": "04V9", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b102d512b25aab9a86083383a809e042fa027f71bd07b64beccaea3b4c238da3", "source_text": "Proves some surprising and interesting results on when an algebraic stack can be reconstructed from its associated functor.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0d2307a0ad7554882205745b7beafb4939ea2aaf408d3213f23a2bb2314425de", "unit_id": "tag:04V9:item002-quote"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "list_item", "parent_tag": "04V9", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\item David Rydh:\n\\emph{", "suffix": "}\n\\cite{rydh_approx}\n\\begin{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1bd3d77de528c0c73e8c3bf7d1c97a915316522ab8e6cb2feea2f43c420fe75a", "source_text": "Noetherian approximation of algebraic spaces and stacks", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7b11084f7b8ca6ca93a10163c5d1d5ef4ef8855c81f9e7c2734f1ef87c3b3135", "unit_id": "tag:04V9:item003"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "quote", "parent_tag": "04V9", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{quote}\n\\end{itemize}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cb10b349b9ffdac4d8539e8155be2fb3f80032d8be563a87a5b46d46b9a68b7c", "source_text": "This paper shows that every quasi-compact algebraic stack with quasi-finite diagonal can be approximated by a Noetherian stack. There are applications to removing the Noetherian hypothesis in results of Chevalley, Serre, Zariski and Chow.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3cca6903a7373311f9a1dcd6e1ac49584b9412d97fb901df1d3c4c39763ca9d1", "unit_id": "tag:04V9:item003-quote"}
